{"id":"mahabharata-6-086","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":86,"title":"षडशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 86 · Eighth day: Shakuni's sons, Iravan's death","summary":{"en":"Shakuni and Kritavarman charge the Pandavas and Arjuna's son Iravan kills Shakuni's brothers. The demon Alambusha then kills Iravan, and the war grows into a savage fight.","kn":"ಶಕುನಿ ಮತ್ತು ಕೃತವರ್ಮ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಮಗ ಇರಾವಾನ್ ಶಕುನಿಯ ತಮ್ಮಂದಿರನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಾಕ್ಷಸ ಅಲಂಬುಷ ಇರಾವಾನನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯುದ್ಧ ಕ್ರೂರವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"शकुनि और कृतवर्मा पाण्डवों पर चढ़ते हैं, और अर्जुन का पुत्र इरावान् शकुनि के भाइयों को मार देता है। फिर राक्षस अलम्बुष इरावान् को मार देता है और युद्ध बर्बर हो उठता है।","te":"శకుని, కృతవర్మ పాండవులపైకి దూకుతారు; అర్జునుని కొడుకు ఇరావంతుడు శకుని సోదరులను చంపుతాడు. రాక్షసుడు అలంబుషుడు ఇరావంతుని చంపుతాడు; యుద్ధం క్రూరమవుతుంది.","ta":"சகுனியும் கிருதவர்மனும் பாண்டவரைத் தாக்க, அர்ஜுனன் மகன் இராவான் சகுனியின் சகோதரர்களைக் கொல்கிறான். அலம்புசன் என்ற அரக்கன் இராவானைக் கொல்ல, போர் கொடூரமாகிறது.","ml":"ശകുനിയും കൃതവർമാവും പാണ്ഡവർക്കെതിരെ പാഞ്ഞടുക്കുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ പുത്രൻ ഇരാവൻ ശകുനിയുടെ സഹോദരന്മാരെ വധിക്കുന്നു. പിന്നീട് അലംബുഷൻ ഇരാവനെ കൊല്ലുന്നു; യുദ്ധം ക്രൂരമായ പോരാട്ടമായി മാറുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.86; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा रौद्रे राजन्वीरवरक्षये ।\nशकुनिः सौबलः श्रीमान्पाण्डवान्समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While this terrible destruction of the best of heroes went on, O king, the glorious Shakuni, son of Subala, charged at the Pandavas."}},{"n":2,"text":"तथैव सात्वतो राजन्हार्दिक्यः परवीरहा ।\nअभ्यद्रवत संग्रामे पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too the Satvata Kritavarman, son of Hridika, slayer of enemy heroes, charged at the Pandava army in the battle."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः काम्बोजमुख्यानां नदीजानां च वाजिनाम् ।\nआरट्टानां महीजानां सिन्धुजानां च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with the horses from every land, the best of the Kamboja horses, the river-bred, the Aratta, the earth-born, the Sindhu-bred,"}},{"n":4,"text":"वनायुजानां शुभ्राणां तथा पर्वतवासिनाम् ।\nये चापरे तित्तिरजा जवना वातरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Vanayu-bred, the white ones, those of mountain dwellers, and others, Tittira-bred and swift as the wind,"}},{"n":5,"text":"सुवर्णालंकृतैरेतैर्वर्मवद्भिः सुकल्पितैः ।\nहयैर्वातजवैर्मुख्यैः पाण्डवस्य सुतो बली ।\nअभ्यवर्तत तत्सैन्यं हृष्टरूपः परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with these well-prepared, armored horses adorned with gold, the best of them swift as the wind, the strong son of the Pandava, glad in appearance and a tormentor of foes, advanced against that army."}},{"n":6,"text":"अर्जुनस्याथ दायाद इरावान्नाम वीर्यवान् ।\nसुतायां नागराजस्य जातः पार्थेन धीमता ॥","meaning":{"en":"This was the heroic Iravan, a son of Arjuna, born of the daughter of the serpent king to wise Partha."}},{"n":7,"text":"ऐरावतेन सा दत्ता अनपत्या महात्मना ।\nपत्यौ हते सुपर्णेन कृपणा दीनचेतना ॥","meaning":{"en":"She had been given to Arjuna by the great-souled Airavata, childless and wretched in mind, her husband having been killed by Suparna."}},{"n":8,"text":"भार्यार्थं तां च जग्राह पार्थः कामवशानुगाम् ।\nएवमेष समुत्पन्नः परक्षेत्रेऽर्जुनात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha took her as his wife, since she followed her desire for him. So this son of Arjuna was born in another's field."}},{"n":9,"text":"स नागलोके संवृद्धो मात्रा च परिरक्षितः ।\nपितृव्येण परित्यक्तः पार्थद्वेषाद्दुरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"He grew up in the world of the nagas, protected by his mother, abandoned by his wicked paternal uncle out of hatred for Partha."}},{"n":10,"text":"रूपवान्वीर्यसंपन्नो गुणवान्सत्यविक्रमः ।\nइन्द्रलोकं जगामाशु श्रुत्वा तत्रार्जुनं गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Handsome, powerful, virtuous and of true valor, he quickly went to Indra's world when he heard that Arjuna had gone there."}},{"n":11,"text":"सोऽभिगम्य महात्मानं पितरं सत्यविक्रमम् ।\nअभ्यवादयदव्यग्रो विनयेन कृताञ्जलिः ।\nइरावानस्मि भद्रं ते पुत्रश्चाहं तवाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"He approached his great-souled father of true prowess, and calmly saluted him with humility, hands joined: \"I am Iravan; may it be well with you. I am your son, O lord.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"मातुः समागमो यश्च तत्सर्वं प्रत्यवेदयत् ।\nतच्च सर्वं यथावृत्तमनुसस्मार पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He told him all about his mother's union with Arjuna, and the Pandava recalled all of it as it had happened."}},{"n":13,"text":"परिष्वज्य सुतं चापि सोऽऽत्मनः सदृशं गुणैः ।\nप्रीतिमानभवत्पार्थो देवराजनिवेशने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embracing his son, who was like himself in qualities, Partha was delighted in the palace of the king of the gods."}},{"n":14,"text":"सोऽर्जुनेन समाज्ञप्तो देवलोके तदा नृप ।\nप्रीतिपूर्वं महाबाहुः स्वकार्यं प्रति भारत ।\nयुद्धकाले त्वयास्माकं साह्यं देयमिति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in the world of the gods, O king, Arjuna charged him lovingly about his own affairs: \"At the time of battle you must help us, my lord.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"बाढमित्येवमुक्त्वा च युद्धकाल उपागतः ।\nकामवर्णजवैरश्वैः संवृतो बहुभिर्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" he had come when the time of battle arrived, surrounded by many horses of whatever color and speed he liked, O king."}},{"n":16,"text":"ते हयाः काञ्चनापीडा नानावर्णा मनोजवाः ।\nउत्पेतुः सहसा राजन्हंसा इव महोदधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those horses, with gold trappings, of many colors, swift as thought, sprang forward suddenly, O king, like swans on a great ocean."}},{"n":17,"text":"ते त्वदीयान्समासाद्य हयसंघान्महाजवान् ।\nक्रोडैः क्रोडानभिघ्नन्तो घोणाभिश्च परस्परम् ।\nनिपेतुः सहसा राजन्सुवेगाभिहता भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting your great, swift droves of horses, they struck one another with chests and with muzzles, and fell suddenly to the ground, hit by their great speed, O king."}},{"n":18,"text":"निपतद्भिस्तथा तैश्च हयसंघैः परस्परम् ।\nशुश्रुवे दारुणः शब्दः सुपर्णपतने यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those droves of horses fell on one another, a terrible sound was heard, as when Garuda swoops down."}},{"n":19,"text":"तथैव च महाराज समेत्यान्योन्यमाहवे ।\nपरस्परवधं घोरं चक्रुस्ते हयसादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way, O great king, the cavalrymen of both sides met in the battle and killed one another terribly."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा वर्तमाने संकुले तुमुले भृशम् ।\nउभयोरपि संशान्ता हयसंघाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that crowded and tumultuous fighting went on, the droves of horses on both sides were finished off all around."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रक्षीणसायकाः शूरा निहताश्वाः श्रमातुराः ।\nविलयं समनुप्राप्तास्तक्षमाणाः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their arrows spent, their horses killed, tired out, the heroes came to rest, hacking at one another."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः क्षीणे हयानीके किंचिच्छेषे च भारत ।\nसौबलस्यात्मजाः शूरा निर्गता रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when the horse division was destroyed and only a little was left, O Bharata, the brave sons of Subala's son came to the front of the battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"वायुवेगसमस्पर्शा जवे वायुसमांस्तथा ।\nआरुह्य शीलसंपन्नान्वयःस्थांस्तुरगोत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounted on the best of horses, well-bred and in their prime, whose touch was like the wind and whose speed was the wind's,"}},{"n":24,"text":"गजो गवाक्षो वृषकश्चर्मवानार्जवः शुकः ।\nषडेते बलसंपन्ना निर्ययुर्महतो बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"these six, Gaja, Gavaksha, Vrishaka, Charmavan, Arjava and Shuka, endowed with strength, rode out from the great army."}},{"n":25,"text":"वार्यमाणाः शकुनिना स्वैश्च योधैर्महाबलैः ।\nसंनद्धा युद्धकुशला रौद्ररूपा महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though held back by Shakuni and his own mighty warriors, they were armed, skilled in fighting, fierce in form and very strong."}},{"n":26,"text":"तदनीकं महाबाहो भित्त्वा परमदुर्जयम् ।\nबलेन महता युक्ताः स्वर्गाय विजयैषिणः ।\nविविशुस्ते तदा हृष्टा गान्धारा युद्धदुर्मदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Breaking through that nearly invincible army, O long-armed one, with a great force, seeking victory and heaven, those Gandharas, wild in battle, entered gladly."}},{"n":27,"text":"तान्प्रविष्टांस्तदा दृष्ट्वा इरावानपि वीर्यवान् ।\nअब्रवीत्समरे योधान्विचित्राभरणायुधान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them enter, the powerful Iravan spoke to his warriors, who had many ornaments and weapons."}},{"n":28,"text":"यथैते धार्तराष्ट्रस्य योधाः सानुगवाहनाः ।\nहन्यन्ते समरे सर्वे तथा नीतिर्विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Make a plan so that these warriors of Dhritarashtra's son, with their followers and mounts, are all killed in the battle."}},{"n":29,"text":"बाढमित्येवमुक्त्वा ते सर्वे योधा इरावतः ।\nजघ्नुस्ते वै परानीकं दुर्जयं समरे परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"Yes,\" all of Iravan's warriors struck that enemy army that others in the battle found hard to beat."}},{"n":30,"text":"तदनीकमनीकेन समरे वीक्ष्य पातितम् ।\nअमृष्यमाणास्ते सर्वे सुबलस्यात्मजा रणे ।\nइरावन्तमभिद्रुत्य सर्वतः पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing their army struck down in the battle by his army, all the sons of Subala, unable to bear it, rushed at Iravan and surrounded him on every side."}},{"n":31,"text":"ताडयन्तः शितैः प्रासैश्चोदयन्तः परस्परम् ।\nते शूराः पर्यधावन्त कुर्वन्तो महदाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Striking him with sharp lances and urging one another on, those heroes ran all around him, making a great uproar."}},{"n":32,"text":"इरावानथ निर्भिन्नः प्रासैस्तीक्ष्णैर्महात्मभिः ।\nस्रवता रुधिरेणाक्तस्तोत्त्रैर्विद्ध इव द्विपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Iravan, pierced by the sharp lances of those great men and drenched in the blood flowing from him, looked like an elephant pierced by goads."}},{"n":33,"text":"उरस्यपि च पृष्ठे च पार्श्वयोश्च भृशाहतः ।\nएको बहुभिरत्यर्थं धैर्याद्राजन्न विव्यथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck hard in the chest, back and sides, though alone against many, he was not troubled, O king, so steady was he."}},{"n":34,"text":"इरावानथ संक्रुद्धः सर्वांस्तान्निशितैः शरैः ।\nमोहयामास समरे विद्ध्वा परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Iravan, furious, bewildered them all, striking them with sharp arrows in the battle, he, conqueror of enemy cities."}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रासानुद्धृत्य सर्वांश्च स्वशरीरादरिंदमः ।\nतैरेव ताडयामास सुबलस्यात्मजान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pulling the lances out of his own body, the tormentor of foes struck the sons of Subala with the very same lances in the battle."}},{"n":36,"text":"निकृष्य निशितं खड्गं गृहीत्वा च शरावरम् ।\nपदातिस्तूर्णमागच्छज्जिघांसुः सौबलान्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drawing a sharp sword and taking a shield, he came on foot in haste, wishing to kill the sons of Subala in the battle."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः प्रत्यागतप्राणाः सर्वे ते सुबलात्मजाः ।\nभूयः क्रोधसमाविष्टा इरावन्तमथाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the sons of Subala, having recovered their senses, flew again in rage at Iravan."}},{"n":38,"text":"इरावानपि खड्गेन दर्शयन्पाणिलाघवम् ।\nअभ्यवर्तत तान्सर्वान्सौबलान्बलदर्पितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Iravan too, proud of his strength, turned on all those sons of Subala, showing the quickness of his hands with the sword."}},{"n":39,"text":"लाघवेनाथ चरतः सर्वे ते सुबलात्मजाः ।\nअन्तरं नाध्यगच्छन्त चरन्तः शीघ्रगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he moved with that quickness, all the sons of Subala, fast-moving as they were, could find no opening."}},{"n":40,"text":"भूमिष्ठमथ तं संख्ये संप्रदृश्य ततः पुनः ।\nपरिवार्य भृशं सर्वे ग्रहीतुमुपचक्रमुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him on the ground in the battle, they all surrounded him closely and set about to seize him."}},{"n":41,"text":"अथाभ्याशगतानां स खड्गेनामित्रकर्शनः ।\nउपहस्तावहस्ताभ्यां तेषां गात्राण्यकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they came near, that tormentor of enemies, using his sword with each hand, cut away their limbs."}},{"n":42,"text":"आयुधानि च सर्वेषां बाहूनपि च भूषितान् ।\nअपतन्त निकृत्ताङ्गा गता भूमिं गतासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Weapons and ornamented arms of all of them fell, and with their limbs cut off they went lifeless to the ground."}},{"n":43,"text":"वृषकस्तु महाराज बहुधा परिविक्षतः ।\nअमुच्यत महारौद्रात्तस्माद्वीरावकर्तनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrishaka alone, O great king, though wounded in many places, escaped from that terrible slaughter of heroes."}},{"n":44,"text":"तान्सर्वान्पतितान्दृष्ट्वा भीतो दुर्योधनस्ततः ।\nअभ्यभाषत संक्रुद्धो राक्षसं घोरदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them all fallen, Duryodhana was afraid, and in anger spoke to the terrible-looking rakshasa,"}},{"n":45,"text":"आर्श्यशृङ्गिं महेष्वासं मायाविनमरिंदमम् ।\nवैरिणं भीमसेनस्य पूर्वं बकवधेन वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alambusa, the great bowman, son of Rishyashringa, magician, tormentor of enemies, who had been Bhima's enemy since the killing of Baka."}},{"n":46,"text":"पश्य वीर यथा ह्येष फल्गुनस्य सुतो बली ।\nमायावी विप्रियं घोरमकार्षीन्मे बलक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See, hero, how this strong son of Phalguna, with his magic, has done me a terrible wrong, destroying my force."}},{"n":47,"text":"त्वं च कामगमस्तात मायास्त्रे च विशारदः ।\nकृतवैरश्च पार्थेन तस्मादेनं रणे जहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, dear one, can go where you wish and are skilled in magic weapons, and you have a feud with Partha. So kill him in the battle."}},{"n":48,"text":"बाढमित्येवमुक्त्वा तु राक्षसो घोरदर्शनः ।\nप्रययौ सिंहनादेन यत्रार्जुनसुतो युवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"Yes,\" the terrible-looking rakshasa went with a lion's roar to where the young son of Arjuna was."}},{"n":49,"text":"स्वारूढैर्युद्धकुशलैर्विमलप्रासयोधिभिः ।\nवीरैः प्रहारिभिर्युक्तः स्वैरनीकैः समावृतः ।\nनिहन्तुकामः समरे इरावन्तं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was surrounded by his own divisions of brave strikers, skilled in battle, well mounted, fighting with bright lances, wanting to kill the mighty Iravan in the battle."}},{"n":50,"text":"इरावानपि संक्रुद्धस्त्वरमाणः पराक्रमी ।\nहन्तुकामममित्रघ्नो राक्षसं प्रत्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Iravan too, enraged, brave, and a slayer of foes, quickly held off the rakshasa who wished to kill him."}},{"n":51,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य राक्षसः सुमहाबलः ।\nत्वरमाणस्ततो मायां प्रयोक्तुमुपचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him come, the very strong rakshasa hurriedly began to use his magic."}},{"n":52,"text":"तेन मायामयाः कॢप्ता हयास्तावन्त एव हि ।\nस्वारूढा राक्षसैर्घोरैः शूलपट्टिशपाणिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By it he made as many illusory horses, ridden by terrible rakshasas with spears and axes in their hands."}},{"n":53,"text":"ते संरब्धाः समागम्य द्विसाहस्राः प्रहारिणः ।\nअचिराद्गमयामासुः प्रेतलोकं परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting in fury, those two thousand strikers soon sent one another to the world of the dead."}},{"n":54,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु निहते सैन्ये तावुभौ युद्धदुर्मदौ ।\nसंग्रामे व्यवतिष्ठेतां यथा वै वृत्रवासवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that force was destroyed, those two, wild in fighting, stood in the battle like Vritra and Indra."}},{"n":55,"text":"आद्रवन्तमभिप्रेक्ष्य राक्षसं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nइरावान्क्रोधसंरब्धः प्रत्यधावन्महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the rakshasa, wild in battle, rushing at him, mighty Iravan, in rage, ran at him."}},{"n":56,"text":"समभ्याशगतस्याजौ तस्य खड्गेन दुर्मतेः ।\nचिच्छेद कार्मुकं दीप्तं शरावापं च पञ्चकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that wicked one came near in the battle, he cut his bright bow with his sword, and the five-fold quiver."}},{"n":57,"text":"स निकृत्तं धनुर्दृष्ट्वा खं जवेन समाविशत् ।\nइरावन्तमभिक्रुद्धं मोहयन्निव मायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his bow cut, the rakshasa flew up quickly into the sky, as if bewildering the furious Iravan with his magic."}},{"n":58,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षमुत्पत्य इरावानपि राक्षसम् ।\nविमोहयित्वा मायाभिस्तस्य गात्राणि सायकैः ।\nचिच्छेद सर्वमर्मज्ञः कामरूपो दुरासदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Iravan too rose up into the sky and, bewildering the rakshasa with his own illusions, that knower of every vital spot, hard to approach and able to take any form, cut his limbs with arrows."}},{"n":59,"text":"तथा स राक्षसश्रेष्ठः शरैः कृत्तः पुनः पुनः ।\nसंबभूव महाराज समवाप च यौवनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though that best of rakshasas was cut again and again by the arrows, O great king, he regained his youth each time."}},{"n":60,"text":"माया हि सहजा तेषां वयो रूपं च कामजम् ।\nएवं तद्राक्षसस्याङ्गं छिन्नं छिन्नं व्यरोहत ॥","meaning":{"en":"For illusion is natural to them, and age and form come as they wish; so the rakshasa's limbs, cut again and again, grew back."}},{"n":61,"text":"इरावानपि संक्रुद्धो राक्षसं तं महाबलम् ।\nपरश्वधेन तीक्ष्णेन चिच्छेद च पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Iravan, enraged, cut that very strong rakshasa again and again with a sharp axe."}},{"n":62,"text":"स तेन बलिना वीरश्छिद्यमान इव द्रुमः ।\nराक्षसो व्यनदद्घोरं स शब्दस्तुमुलोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut by that strong hero like a tree, the rakshasa roared terribly, and the sound was tumultuous."}},{"n":63,"text":"परश्वधक्षतं रक्षः सुस्राव रुधिरं बहु ।\nततश्चुक्रोध बलवांश्चक्रे वेगं च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded by the axe, the rakshasa bled heavily, and then, strong as he was, grew angry and moved with speed in the battle."}},{"n":64,"text":"आर्श्यशृङ्गिस्ततो दृष्ट्वा समरे शत्रुमूर्जितम् ।\nकृत्वा घोरं महद्रूपं ग्रहीतुमुपचक्रमे ।\nसंग्रामशिरसो मध्ये सर्वेषां तत्र पश्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his mighty enemy in the battle, Alambusa took on a terrible, huge form and set about to seize him, in the head of the battle in the middle of all, with everyone watching."}},{"n":65,"text":"तां दृष्ट्वा तादृशीं मायां राक्षसस्य महात्मनः ।\nइरावानपि संक्रुद्धो मायां स्रष्टुं प्रचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great-souled rakshasa's magic like that, Iravan too, enraged, set about to create illusion."}},{"n":66,"text":"तस्य क्रोधाभिभूतस्य संयुगेष्वनिवर्तिनः ।\nयोऽन्वयो मातृकस्तस्य स एनमभिपेदिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he was overcome with rage and never turned back in battles, the kin of his mother's line came to him."}},{"n":67,"text":"स नागैर्बहुशो राजन्सर्वतः संवृतो रणे ।\nदधार सुमहद्रूपमनन्त इव भोगवान् ।\nततो बहुविधैर्नागैश्छादयामास राक्षसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on every side in the battle by many nagas, O king, he took on a huge form like the serpent Ananta, and covered the rakshasa with many kinds of serpents."}},{"n":68,"text":"छाद्यमानस्तु नागैः स ध्यात्वा राक्षसपुंगवः ।\nसौपर्णं रूपमास्थाय भक्षयामास पन्नगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the nagas covered him, the foremost of rakshasas thought it over, took the form of Garuda, and devoured the serpents."}},{"n":69,"text":"मायया भक्षिते तस्मिन्नन्वये तस्य मातृके ।\nविमोहितमिरावन्तमसिना राक्षसोऽवधीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When his mother's line had been devoured by illusion, the rakshasa killed the bewildered Iravan with a sword."}},{"n":70,"text":"सकुण्डलं समुकुटं पद्मेन्दुसदृशप्रभम् ।\nइरावतः शिरो रक्षः पातयामास भूतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasa brought Iravan's head down to the ground, with its earrings and crown, bright as the lotus and the moon."}},{"n":71,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु निहते वीरे राक्षसेनार्जुनात्मजे ।\nविशोकाः समपद्यन्त धार्तराष्ट्राः सराजकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Arjuna's son, the hero, had been killed by the rakshasa, Dhritarashtra's sons and their kings were freed of grief."}},{"n":72,"text":"तस्मिन्महति संग्रामे तादृशे भैरवे पुनः ।\nमहान्व्यतिकरो घोरः सेनयोः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that great, fearful battle there arose a great and terrible disorder in both armies."}},{"n":73,"text":"हया गजाः पदाताश्च विमिश्रा दन्तिभिर्हताः ।\nरथाश्च दन्तिनश्चैव पत्तिभिस्तत्र सूदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses, elephants and foot soldiers were mixed together and killed by elephants; chariots and elephants were destroyed there by foot soldiers."}},{"n":74,"text":"तथा पत्तिरथौघाश्च हयाश्च बहवो रणे ।\nरथिभिर्निहता राजंस्तव तेषां च संकुले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise masses of foot soldiers, chariots and many horses were killed by charioteers in that crowded fight, among your men and theirs, O king."}},{"n":75,"text":"अजानन्नर्जुनश्चापि निहतं पुत्रमौरसम् ।\nजघान समरे शूरान्राज्ञस्तान्भीष्मरक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, not knowing that his own son was killed, struck down in the battle those brave kings who guarded Bhishma."}},{"n":76,"text":"तथैव तावका राजन्सृञ्जयाश्च महाबलाः ।\nजुह्वतः समरे प्राणान्निजघ्नुरितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise your men and the mighty Srinjayas offered up their lives in the battle and killed one another."}},{"n":77,"text":"मुक्तकेशा विकवचा विरथाश्छिन्नकार्मुकाः ।\nबाहुभिः समयुध्यन्त समवेताः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With loosened hair, without armor, without chariots, their bows cut, they fought each other together with their bare arms."}},{"n":78,"text":"तथा मर्मातिगैर्भीष्मो निजघान महारथान् ।\nकम्पयन्समरे सेनां पाण्डवानां महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Bhishma, the mighty, with arrows that pierced vital parts, killed great chariot-warriors, making the Pandava army shake in the battle."}},{"n":79,"text":"तेन यौधिष्ठिरे सैन्ये बहवो मानवा हताः ।\nदन्तिनः सादिनश्चैव रथिनोऽथ हयास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By him many men in Yudhishthira's army were killed, elephants, cavalrymen, charioteers and horses."}},{"n":80,"text":"तत्र भारत भीष्मस्य रणे दृष्ट्वा पराक्रमम् ।\nअत्यद्भुतमपश्याम शक्रस्येव पराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhishma's prowess in the battle, O Bharata, we saw something very marvelous, like the prowess of Indra."}},{"n":81,"text":"तथैव भीमसेनस्य पार्षतस्य च भारत ।\nरौद्रमासीत्तदा युद्धं सात्वतस्य च धन्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise there was a terrible fight of Bhimasena and Prishata's son with the Satvata archer."}},{"n":82,"text":"दृष्ट्वा द्रोणस्य विक्रान्तं पाण्डवान्भयमाविशत् ।\nएक एव रणे शक्तो हन्तुमस्मान्ससैनिकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Drona's valor, fear entered the Pandavas: this one man alone is able to kill us with our soldiers in the battle."}},{"n":83,"text":"किं पुनः पृथिवीशूरैर्योधव्रातैः समावृतः ।\nइत्यब्रुवन्महाराज रणे द्रोणेन पीडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What then when he is surrounded by hosts of warriors, heroes of the earth? So they said, O great king, pressed by Drona in the battle."}},{"n":84,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा रौद्रे संग्रामे भरतर्षभ ।\nउभयोः सेनयोः शूरा नामृष्यन्त परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the terrible battle went on, O best of Bharatas, the warriors of both armies could not bear one another."}},{"n":85,"text":"आविष्टा इव युध्यन्ते रक्षोभूता महाबलाः ।\nतावकाः पाण्डवेयाश्च संरब्धास्तात धन्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty ones fought as if possessed, like rakshasas, your men and the Pandavas, enraged archers, dear one."}},{"n":86,"text":"न स्म पश्यामहे कंचिद्यः प्राणान्परिरक्षति ।\nसंग्रामे दैत्यसंकाशे तस्मिन्योद्धा नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw no one who guarded his life in that battle, which was like that of the daityas, lord of men."}}]}]}